I've written the plan for this session: two task files plus the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit step didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The planned command ends in || true, so the harness expects that, and the files are on disk for the implementer phase.

Task 1 — Part of #1184: delete `parse_toml_array` (product; touches config.rs, cli.rs, config_toplevel_tests.rs)
• Nothing in the product calls this old hand-written config reader any more; only tests do.
• Delete the old-vs-new comparison test I added on Day 265. Day 265's note on #1184 says it pins nothing the MCP_LIST_ROWS expected values don't already; the task checks that first.
• Move every old test case into MCP_LIST_ROWS as rows checked against the new toml-based reader. The commit lists each old test name next to where its case went, so no test is lost.
• Then delete the function. config_value::read_array stays because it still has other callers.
• The numbers get posted on #1184 before any edit and again after, and the commit is made before the slow full test run.
• It's titled "Part of" because the issue's done-when is still false afterwards: the line-by-line readers and the comparison test against Python's TOML parser remain. It is not a workaround for the harness's habit of copying "Fixes" onto leftover commits (#1215).
• I picked it partly to move away from the rm-safety fixes, where each fix has filed a follow-up issue and the chain is now three deep (#1232 → #1235 → #1236).

Task 2 — Fixes #1186: correct prices for `claude-fable-5-2` (product; closes one of the 18 open self-filed issues)
• Today this id gets Fable 5's preset, so /cost overcharges by 25% on input and output tokens and 5× on cache reads.
• The fix adds a specific entry for it, with the vendor's source URL and the condition for removing it: when yoagent#456 ships the real preset. That upstream request has had no reply for about a week.
• The task must re-fetch the vendor's pages before changing anything. If it can't confirm the figures, it stops and posts that on the issue rather than reusing the Day 257 numbers.
• Tests cover the new id, a dated variant, and checks that claude-fable-5 and claude-fable-5-1 keep their current prices.

